# Usage:
#   pea.py --input <file.lpe|file.wpe> [--profile <json>] [--kb <json>]
#           [--output <file>] [--dry-run] [--verbose] [--log] [--hashmap]
#
# Description:
#   PEA processes PEASS output files. It auto-detects the type by extension:
#     - .lpe → LinPEAS (Linux) → uses existing LPA modules (lpa-*) and profiles
#     - .wpe → WinPEAS (Windows) → NOT SUPPORTED YET (clean message)
#
#   In Linux mode, PEA behaves like LPA: it loads PKB/SKB, routes to lpa-*
#   modules, groups findings, and renders a full text report identical in
#   structure to LPA.
#
# Output Files:
#   /var/log/pea.py.log            (when --log is used)
#   .hashmap/pea.py.hash           (when --hashmap is used)
#   .hashmap/pea.py.timestamp      (when --hashmap is used)
#
# End Help

